<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<modification>
    <id>TropaTT CRM gateway order hook</id>
    <version>1.0.1</version>
    <vqmver>2.0</vqmver>
    <author>Anton Barinov</author>

    <!--
      OpenCart 1.5.x has neither OCMOD (2.0+) nor the model event table (2.3+),
      so the order hook is installed by vQmod:

        1. make sure vQmod is installed in the shop (the `vqmod/` directory at
           the OpenCart root with `vqmod/vqmod.php` included from index.php and
           admin/index.php);
        2. copy `vqmod/xml/tropatt.xml` into the shop's `vqmod/xml/` directory
           (the archive already places it there);
        3. open the storefront and the admin once so vQmod regenerates its
           cache, then install the module in Extensions → Modules.

      vQmod injects the call into `catalog/model/checkout/order.php` right after the
      signature of the two methods that *change an order status* in a 1.5 storefront:

        confirm($order_id, $order_status_id, $comment = '', $notify = false)  (line 159)
        update($order_id, $order_status_id, $comment = '', $notify = false)   (line 583)

      `addOrderHistory()` does not exist in that file - it is an admin-side method of
      OpenCart 2.x with a different signature (`addOrderHistory($order_id, $data)`) -
      so the previous search string never matched and the modification was silently
      not applied: no order ever left a 1.5 shop for the CRM.

      The order row exists at that point and the new status travels in the arguments,
      so the payload carries the right status even though the UPDATE below has not
      run yet. `ModelModuleTropatt::handleOrderStatusChange()` decides whether the
      push happens (module enabled, echo guard off); the model - not the controller -
      owns the flag, because injected model code cannot reach controller state.

      The push is idempotent on the CRM side (`X-TropaTT-Idempotency-Key` =
      `{store_key}:order:{order_id}`), so a retry never creates a duplicate.
    -->
    <file name="catalog/model/checkout/order.php">
        <operation>
            <search position="after"><![CDATA[public function confirm($order_id, $order_status_id]]></search>
            <add><![CDATA[
		// TropaTT CRM hook: push the order and its new status to the gateway.
		if ($this->config->get('module_tropatt_status')) {
			$this->load->model('module/tropatt');
			$this->model_module_tropatt->handleOrderStatusChange($order_id, $order_status_id);
		}
]]></add>
        </operation>
        <operation>
            <search position="after"><![CDATA[public function update($order_id, $order_status_id]]></search>
            <add><![CDATA[
		// TropaTT CRM hook: push the order and its new status to the gateway.
		if ($this->config->get('module_tropatt_status')) {
			$this->load->model('module/tropatt');
			$this->model_module_tropatt->handleOrderStatusChange($order_id, $order_status_id);
		}
]]></add>
        </operation>
    </file>
</modification>
